# Stub rules for github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web (the rt module in this
# repository; it has no version tag, so the rules are checked against the
# source at rt/web/web.go).
#
# The route functions are generic: Get[In, Out any](r *Router, pattern string,
# h func(context.Context, In) (Out, error)) (web.go:337-357). The route rule
# names the origin, which matches every instantiation. Argument 0 is the
# *Router, argument 1 the pattern (the path) and argument 2 the handler, counted
# from 0. The method is fixed by the function: Get is GET, Post POST, Put PUT,
# Patch PATCH and Delete DELETE.
route github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Get GET 1 2       # web.go:337
route github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Post POST 1 2     # web.go:342
route github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Put PUT 1 2       # web.go:347
route github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Patch PATCH 1 2   # web.go:352
route github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Delete DELETE 1 2 # web.go:357

# Effects of the registration and option functions of rt/web. A stub applies at
# every call site, so the rules replace what the analysis would see through the
# router's function-valued fields (unknown). Each rule states what the function does
# itself; the function values it stores are called later, or by the function
# itself where the comment says so.
#
# New and the options: they only build a Router from its arguments
# (web.go:126 New, :68 WithMiddleware, :74 WithErrorEncoder, :80 WithLogger). The one call made
# here is the middleware given to WithMiddleware, which New wraps around the
# handler; that middleware is a function value of the caller and its effects are
# not in this rule. The error encoder and the logger are called at request time.
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.New pure
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.WithMiddleware pure         # web.go:69 r.mw = append(r.mw, mw...)
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.WithErrorEncoder pure      # web.go:75 r.encodeErr = fn
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.WithLogger pure            # web.go:81 r.logger = l
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.WithPanicHandler panic     # web.go:93-96 panics on a nil function; then r.panicFn = fn
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.WithMaxBody panic          # web.go:104-107 panics when n <= 0; then r.maxBody = n

# The route functions register the route and return. register (web.go:363) panics on
# a nil handler, an output or input that schema.Compile rejects, a bad pattern, and
# a pattern that mux.HandleFunc refuses (a conflict). It never calls the handler:
# the handler is stored in the mux's closure, and runs per request. The check
# cache of schema.Compile is not an effect in the taxonomy (rt/schema keeps the
# package pure), so it is not listed.
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Get panic                   # web.go:337
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Post panic                  # web.go:342
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Put panic                   # web.go:347
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Patch panic                 # web.go:352
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.Delete panic                # web.go:357

# ErrorBody (web.go:250) encodes an error with json.Marshal and reflection, and reads
# its status through the statusError interface. The StatusCode and MarshalJSON of
# the error are methods of the caller's type and are not included here; the rule
# states the framework's own effects, and it writes nothing (the caller writes).
effects github.com/faintghost/effectgo/rt/web.ErrorBody pure             # web.go:250
